hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17936","Zayd ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Qays al-Judhami, a man who had companionship, he said, The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The martyr is given six qualities at the first drop of his blood: all sins are expiated for him, he is shown his seat in Paradise, he is married from the fair-eyed maidens, he is secured from the greatest terror and from the punishment of the grave, and he is adorned with the garment of faith."
